    How do you know if your sample is large enough?

    Determining the appropriate sample size requires
    a balance between the resources available and
    the benefits of increasing the sample size.
    Large samples provide more accurate results than
    small ones, but the benefit is not as dramatic
    as many people expect, because the precision of
    a survey's estimates increase with the square
    root of the sample size. In other words, a
    sample of 100,000 provides estimates that are
    only about twice as precise as a sample of 2,000
    (a square root of 100 as compared to a square
    root of about 45).

